- **O2 CSV-5 + TSV-5 DONE (2026-11-02)** — inverse-map-based shift optimization for deleteRow (o2_prompts.md #33, Critical; scope shared CSV+TSV): Applied CSV-5 optimization to DelimitedIndexManager.deleteRow() — replaced O(n) entry-set scan with O(1) positionToRowIdMap lookup and O(n) inverse-map shift (lines 478-484). Updated compaction threshold check to use `positionToRowIdMap.size()` for O(1) complexity (line 485). **Key improvements**: (1) Single deleteRow: O(1) positionToRowId lookup (CSV-1 foundation) + O(n) inverse-map shift with cache-friendly contiguous Integer operations; (2) Bulk window deletes: O(1) per mirror removal + single O(n log n) reindex; (3) Tail-position deletes: O(1) no-shift path. **Verification**: Created `BatchDeleteIsONTest.java` @Tag(storage) @StorageType({csv,tsv}) with 3 test methods demonstrating linear time complexity for batch operations. **Acceptance tests**: `LazyDeleteTest` 18/0, `CsvStorageTest` 18/0 pass — confirms CSV/TSV storage functionality intact. Files: `diesel/storage/DelimitedIndexManager.java` (inverse-map shift optimization + size check), `src/test/java/diesel/BatchDeleteIsONTest.java` (new test class). Gates: compile OK; LazyDeleteTest 18/0, CsvStorageTest 18/0; **core acceptance green**; timing-quick SKIP (not JOIN/performance path). TIA: `DelimitedIndexManager.java;storage-csv,storage-tsv` + `BatchDeleteIsONTest.java;storage` in mapping. TODO: CSV-6 (#27), JSONL-2 (#36).